    CVaR risk swap + behavioral probe (branch cvar-risk)
    
    Swap the one-sided directional risk coefficient from VaR (Phi^{-1}(alpha)) to
    CVaR / expected-shortfall (phi(Phi^{-1}(alpha))/(1-alpha)) via new
    cvar_coefficient(). At alpha=0.95: 1.645 -> 2.063 (1.25x margin).
    
    Add tests/micro_dro_probe.cpp: a fast deterministic before/after probe of the
    DRO risk vector + Q* reweighting on the canonical 6-mode scenario, since the
    full experiment suites time out (>280s).
    
    Result (CVAR_RISK_BEHAVIOR.md): CVaR inflates every mode's risk uniformly by
    +0.070 but PRESERVES the risk ranking, so Q* is identical (100% decelerating)
    and only the absolute worst_case_risk rises 0.786 -> 0.856. Confirms Q38: the
    LP reweighting is invariant to a monotone risk-measure change.
    
    Build wiring for the probe (2-line add_executable in CMakeLists.txt) left
    unstaged to avoid bundling unrelated uncommitted test-target additions already
    present in the working tree.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

